@startuml
' ============================================================================
'  E-Compra — Sequence Diagram
'  Revision 2 · 2026-11-12
'  Applies every ruling in docs/DESIGN_DECISIONS.md (see docs/DESIGN_REVIEW.md
'  for the findings). Revision 1 is preserved in ./archive-v1-original/.
'
'  STATUS OWNERSHIP (single authority per fact):
'    Order.status      = the order lifecycle, customer-facing
'    Payment.status    = settlement of one payment attempt
'    DeliveryBooking.status = courier progress
'  Transaction carries no status of its own.
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #526B7A
  LifeLineBorderColor #96AAB5
  LifeLineBackgroundColor white
  ParticipantBorderColor #36546C
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F1F7
}

actor Customer
actor Vendor
boundary "Vue UI" as UI
control "Django REST API" as API
control "Order / Payment Service" as OrderSvc
control "Vendor POS Service" as PosSvc
database MySQL as DB
participant "Payment Gateway" as PG
participant "Delivery Provider" as DP

' ================= Customer: Place Order (multi-vendor split) =================
Customer -> UI: review cart & choose fulfillment
UI -> API: POST /api/orders/ (cart, fulfillment_type, notes, Idempotency-Key)
API -> OrderSvc: authenticate + verify ownership + check Idempotency-Key
alt Idempotency-Key already used by this user
  OrderSvc --> API: 200 + the orders created by that first request
  API --> UI: existing order(s) - no duplicates created
else New request
  OrderSvc -> DB: read cart items + current prices / vendors
  DB --> OrderSvc: cart items (grouped by vendor)
  alt Cart empty / invalid
    API --> UI: HTTP 400 Cart is empty
    UI --> Customer: show correction message
  else Cart valid
    loop For each vendor in cart (multi-vendor split)
      OrderSvc -> DB: create ONE Order (vendor set, status PENDING_PAYMENT)
      OrderSvc -> DB: create OrderItems (unit_price snapshotted)
      OrderSvc -> DB: create linked Transaction (transaction_type, reference_no)
      DB --> OrderSvc: order id per vendor
    end
    alt Fulfillment = PICKUP reservation (no online payment)
      OrderSvc -> DB: set each Order.status = CONFIRMED (reservation accepted)
      OrderSvc -> DB: set Transaction.transaction_type = PICKUP_RESERVATION
      DB --> OrderSvc: reservations confirmed
    else Fulfillment = paid online order
      OrderSvc -> DB: set Transaction.transaction_type = ONLINE_ORDER
      DB --> OrderSvc: pending payment
    end
    OrderSvc -> DB: clear ordered items from cart
    DB --> OrderSvc: cart cleared
    OrderSvc --> API: 201 Created + list of orders (one per vendor)
    API --> UI: order(s) created
    UI --> Customer: show order confirmation / reservation reference
  end
end

' ================= Customer: Verify Payment =================
Customer -> UI: trigger payment verification
UI -> API: POST /api/orders/{id}/verify-payment/
API -> OrderSvc: verify_payment(order, reference)
OrderSvc -> PG: query / verify payment (provider-specific)
PG --> OrderSvc: payment outcome
alt Payment successful
  OrderSvc -> DB: create/update Payment (status VERIFIED, provider_reference)
  OrderSvc -> DB: advance Order.status PENDING_PAYMENT -> CONFIRMED
  DB --> OrderSvc: updated records
  OrderSvc --> API: payment verified + order confirmed
  API --> UI: 200 + confirmed order
  UI --> Customer: show payment confirmation
else Payment failed
  OrderSvc -> DB: record Payment (status FAILED)
  OrderSvc -> DB: leave Order.status = PENDING_PAYMENT (not fulfilable)
  DB --> OrderSvc: updated records
  OrderSvc --> API: payment failed
  API --> UI: not paid
  UI --> Customer: show retry / status message
end

' ================= Customer: Book Delivery =================
Customer -> UI: request delivery booking
UI -> API: POST /api/orders/{id}/book-delivery/
API -> OrderSvc: book_delivery(order)  (delivery orders only)
alt Delivery booking succeeds
  OrderSvc -> DP: request quote / booking
  DP --> OrderSvc: booking reference + tracking + status
  OrderSvc -> DB: create DeliveryBooking (status BOOKED) linked to Transaction
  OrderSvc --> API: delivery booked
  API --> UI: 200 + delivery details
  UI --> Customer: show confirmation & tracking
else Delivery booking fails
  OrderSvc -> DB: create DeliveryBooking (status FAILED)
  OrderSvc --> API: delivery needs attention
  API --> UI: paid order; delivery needs retry
  UI --> Customer: show delivery issue (do not re-charge)
end

' ================= Vendor: Sign in =================
Vendor -> UI: login (username, password)
UI -> API: POST /api/auth/login/ (credentials)
API -> DB: authenticate + read catalog.Vendor via user
DB --> API: vendor storefront (or none)
API --> UI: user data + is_vendor=true + vendor id
UI --> Vendor: redirect to vendor POS dashboard

' ================= Vendor: POS Flow (pickup orders) =================
Vendor -> UI: view orders awaiting handling
UI -> API: GET /api/pos/orders/
API -> PosSvc: list own CONFIRMED orders (prefetch items)
PosSvc -> DB: read orders WHERE vendor = me AND status = CONFIRMED
DB --> PosSvc: orders (paid-online AND pickup reservations)
PosSvc --> API: 200 + order list
API --> UI: order list
UI --> Vendor: show orders (status badges)

Vendor -> UI: select order + click "Prepare"
UI -> API: POST /api/pos/orders/{id}/prepare/
API -> PosSvc: mark order PREPARING + create/update VendorTx
PosSvc -> DB: update Order.status = PREPARING
DB --> PosSvc: updated
PosSvc --> API: 200 + VendorTransaction
API --> UI: updated
UI --> Vendor: show PREPARING badge

Vendor -> UI: click "Ready for Pickup"
UI -> API: POST /api/pos/orders/{id}/ready/
API -> PosSvc: mark order READY_FOR_PICKUP
PosSvc -> DB: update Order.status = READY_FOR_PICKUP
DB --> PosSvc: updated
PosSvc --> API: 200 + VendorTransaction
API --> UI: updated
UI --> Vendor: show READY_FOR_PICKUP badge

Vendor -> UI: record cash payment (cash tendered)
UI -> API: POST /api/pos/orders/{id}/cash-payment/ {cash_tendered}
API -> PosSvc: validate cash_tendered >= order.total_amount
alt Cash sufficient
  PosSvc -> DB: create Payment (provider CASH, status VERIFIED, amount = total)
  PosSvc -> DB: set VendorTx.receipt_serial = RC-{reference_no}-{receipt_attempt}
  PosSvc -> DB: set VendorTx.receipt_attempt = 1 (or +1 on reprint)
  Note over PosSvc: Order.status is NOT changed - cash is a payment event, not a lifecycle step
  PosSvc --> API: change = cash_tendered - total_amount
  API --> UI: 200 + change due + receipt serial
  UI --> Vendor: show change + BIR-style receipt preview
else Cash insufficient
  API --> UI: HTTP 400 amount less than total
  UI --> Vendor: show error
end

Vendor -> UI: click "Confirm Pickup"
UI -> API: POST /api/pos/orders/{id}/confirm-pickup/
API -> PosSvc: validate order.status in CONFIRMED | PREPARING | READY_FOR_PICKUP
alt Valid status
  PosSvc -> DB: advance Order.status -> COMPLETED
  PosSvc -> DB: create/update VendorTx (status COMPLETED)
  DB --> PosSvc: completed
  PosSvc --> API: 200 + order + VendorTransaction
  API --> UI: order completed
  UI --> Vendor: show order completed + receipt
else Invalid status
  API --> UI: HTTP 400 invalid status transition
  UI --> Vendor: show error
end

' ================= Vendor: Delivery order progress =================
Vendor -> UI: click "Out for Delivery" (DELIVERY orders only)
UI -> API: POST /api/pos/orders/{id}/out-for-delivery/
API -> PosSvc: validate fulfillment = DELIVERY and status in CONFIRMED | PREPARING
PosSvc -> DB: update Order.status = OUT_FOR_DELIVERY
PosSvc -> DB: update DeliveryBooking.status = IN_TRANSIT
DB --> PosSvc: updated
PosSvc --> API: 200 + order
API --> UI: updated
UI --> Vendor: show OUT_FOR_DELIVERY badge

Vendor -> UI: click "Delivered" (DELIVERY orders only)
UI -> API: POST /api/pos/orders/{id}/delivered/
API -> PosSvc: validate status = OUT_FOR_DELIVERY
PosSvc -> DB: advance Order.status -> COMPLETED
PosSvc -> DB: update DeliveryBooking.status = DELIVERED, delivered_at = NOW()
DB --> PosSvc: completed
PosSvc --> API: 200 + order
API --> UI: order completed
UI --> Vendor: show order completed

note over PosSvc, DB
  Vendor POS flows are vendor-scoped: a vendor can only act on
  orders they fulfill (catalog.Vendor). Every guard reads
  Order.status - the single lifecycle authority.
  receipt_serial lives on vendors.VendorTransaction, not on Payment,
  and is stable across reprints because receipt_attempt is stored.
end note

note over Customer, PG
  Verify payment server-side. A redirect alone is not proof of payment.
  Payment is idempotent through unique (provider, provider_reference),
  and order creation is idempotent through the Idempotency-Key header,
  so a double-submitted checkout cannot double-charge.
end note

@enduml
